From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: Find drives by their roots when none are
 published.

GetLogicalDrives lists the \DosDevices\ object directory, where the mount
manager publishes each drive. A prefix that runs without that service (a
PS5 title cannot start one) has an empty directory, so GetLogicalDrives
and GetLogicalDriveStrings report no drives at all, while GetDriveType
and paths on the same drives work. A game that picks a drive from this
list finds none.

When the directory holds no drive, open each letter's root, as
GetDriveType does, and leave the last error as it was.
---
 dlls/kernelbase/volume.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/volume.c b/dlls/kernelbase/volume.c
index edfd777..c14515c 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/volume.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/volume.c
@@ -516,6 +516,20 @@ DWORD WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH GetLogicalDrives(void)
         NtClose( handle );
     }
 
+    if (!bitmask)  /* nothing has published the drives: ask for each root */
+    {
+        WCHAR root[] = L"A:\\";
+        DWORD error = GetLastError();
+
+        for (; root[0] <= 'Z'; root[0]++)
+        {
+            if (!open_device_root( root, &handle )) continue;
+            bitmask |= 1 << (root[0] - 'A');
+            NtClose( handle );
+        }
+        SetLastError( error );
+    }
+
     return bitmask;
 }
 
